Rāma recalls Bharata kin grief and trampled camp ground --- Rāma departs with Sītā and Lakṣmaṇa for elsewhere --- Rāma bows at Atri āśrama and wins sonlike welcome --- Atri hosts Rāma and comforts Lakṣmaṇa and Sītā --- Atri calls aged wife and bids Sītā approach Anasūyā --- Atri tells ten-year drought roots fruits and Jāhnavī feat --- Atri tells ten-thousand-year tapas and ten-night feat --- Sītā nears trembling white-haired Anasūyā and asks health --- Anasūyā teaches husband supreme deity above kin --- Anasūyā says virtuous wives following forest reach heaven